PRC-01 Purchase-to-Pay Process Overview

Version: September 2026 · Owner: Procurement Operations · Status: Current


PURPOSE
This overview describes the five stages a purchase moves through at Northstar Services, from the first request to the release of payment. It is an orientation document; it does not set approval limits.

P1 — REQUEST
The requester records the business need before any commitment is made.

P2 — PURCHASE ORDER
Procurement issues an approved purchase order. The purchase order is the purchasing instruction to the supplier.

P3 — RECEIPT
Receiving records receipt of the goods or services. The receipt is the evidence of delivery.

P4 — INVOICE MATCHING
Accounts Payable (AP) matches the supplier invoice to the purchase order and the receipt. An invoice without a recorded receipt goes to the AP exception queue.

P5 — PAYMENT RELEASE
Treasury releases payment only after a separate, authorized payment approval. Matching an invoice (P4) is not an approval to pay.

GLOSSARY
Term | Meaning in this document
Purchase order | Purchasing instruction
Receipt | Evidence of delivery
Invoice | Supplier payment request
Payment approval | Separate authority to release funds

NOT COVERED BY THIS DOCUMENT
Approval thresholds (amount limits) and the holiday calendar are not specified here. Do not infer them from other documents.

Northstar Services is a fictional company. All names, figures, and dates are training material.
